{
  "_about": "Townsfolk. `level` shows on their portrait and tooltip. An npc may keep a shop, be a smith (`forge`: reforges and punches sockets; see forge.json), an enchanter (`enchanter`: enchants gear a rank at a time and scraps it into dust and gems; see enchanting.json), a jeweller (`jeweller`: makes and sets gems; see gems.json), keep the bank (`banker`: opens your bank vault, see Bank), keep an inn (`innkeeper`: you can rent a bed for the night, `bedPrice` coins or CONFIG.inn.bedPrice, to wake whole and rested, or make it your home), train skills (skills.json names its trainer) and has a dialogue (dialogue.json); quests name their giver. `mapIcon` puts their trade on the minimap: vendor, blacksmith, fishing, cooking, innkeeper or trainer (a class trainer). Where they stand is in world.json (npcSpawns); a spawn with `goneWhen` (a condition, such as a story flag) is absent while it holds. `tint` tells apart townsfolk who share a model. `routine` gives them hours to keep by the world clock: the id of a timetable in `routines`, or their own list of blocks. A block is {from: hour 0-24, at: place}, kept from that hour until the next block; places are work (their post), inn (a seat in the nearest inn), home (the nearest house: they go in for the night and answer a knock), or a name in their spawn's `places` ({name: [x, z]}). A spawn's `home` [x, z] names their door. No routine: they stand at their post all day (boards, bankers, innkeepers).",
